REGIONAL REGULATION OF THE SPECIAL CAPITAL REGION PROVINCE

OF JAKARTA

NUMBER 8 OF 2011

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

GOVERNOR OF THE SPECIAL CAPITAL REGION PROVINCE OF JAKARTA,

Considering a. that discrimination and violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights, and crimes against humanity, and are not in accordance with the position of the Special Capital Region Province of Jakarta as the Capital of the Unitary State of the Republic of Indonesia;

Bearing in mind
b. that in the context of fulfilling the constitutional rights of women and children and to improve the quality of life of women and children is one of the mandatory affairs that is the duty, authority, and responsibility of the Regional Government;

c. that discrimination and violence against women and children in the Special Capital Region Province of Jakarta continues to increase and spread, causing members of the community to be unsafe in carrying out their lives, so that integrated protection efforts are needed;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children from Acts of Violence;

