CHAPTER II

PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

Article 2

Protection of women and children from acts of violence shall be conducted based on the principles of:

a. humanity;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. protection;
d. best interests of women and children; and
e. non-discrimination.

Article 3

The objectives of the protection of women and children from acts of violence are to:

a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;
d. provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses; and
e. facilitate and mediate household disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.

CHAPTER III

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 4

Women and children victims of acts of violence shall receive the following rights:

a. the right to be respected for their dignity as human beings;
b. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to compensation;
g. the right to social rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;

the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and

i. j. the right to accompaniment.

Article 5

Child victims of acts of violence, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 4, shall also receive special rights, as follows:

a. the right to respect and full use for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and
e. the right to obtain freedom;

Article 7

1. The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 6 letter a, include:a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence established by the government;
b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with regional financial capacity; andf. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.
2. In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Governor establishes programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in one Regional Action Plan as a basis for SKPD and UKPD in implementing the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
3. The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), constitutes part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).
4. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be regulated by a Governor Regulation.

CHAPTER V

PREVENTION OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 10

1. To prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government conducts empowerment and awareness-raising to families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.
2. In addition to empowerment and awareness-raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government undertakes efforts as follows:: a. increasing the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;
c. opening employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and concern for the prevention of protection of women and children from acts of violence.  e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children; dang. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.

Article 11

1. Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 10, shall be implemented by SKPD and UKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual; dang. public order and security.
2. Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD and UKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

CHAPTER VI

SERVICES FOR VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 12

1. Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence, are as follows:a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal assistance;
d. repatriation;
e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medicolegal;
f. identification services; dang. psychological services.
2. Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the government and implemented by SKPD and UKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection;
d. mental and spiritual;
3. In carrying out the duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government cooperates with government agencies, other regional governments, and the community.
4. Further provisions regarding the procedures for handling services for women and children from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3), shall be regulated by a Governor Regulation.

